igger when the player  walks by with cold war it's possible you  spend so much time with one character in  their dialogue that you miss a  conversation with the other characters  and speaking of that interaction within  missions it's possible to hear different  lines than what other players heard  making the missions feel more unique and  worth playing again  good work don't think anyone saw you  follow me  that's your low profile belt god help us  all  follow me within the safe house is the  evidence board which is a small yet  fantastic touch as it makes the player  choose when to play the mission rather  than force them to cod sometimes can  feel like a story intertwined between  new missions that you just appear in but  cold war lets the player go to the  mission they want making it feel more  real as if you purposely selected this  mission the evidence board's design is  also a nice touch as every mission you  complete is another section of  information gathered all leading to  perseus gold war could simply have given  the player these missions back to back  without any reward for it but the  ability to not only select the mission  you want but look over the current and  past missions evidence makes it feel  like a real investigation  the safe house is also where these  doubts and suspicions come in every  character has certain dialogue options  that either give you vague answers or  just outright not give you an answer at  all  asking where we came from and why we  were selected for the team is a constant  dialogue option and it's confusing every  time as everyone in the safehouse is a  completely different and unrelated  reason this is where the suspicion of my  own team started for me as something  felt off i just couldn't figure out what  or why but all good investigations need  a starting point which is why the team  asks each other to remember their time  in vietnam when they first met perseus  this then enters a common theme with  black ops a vietnam mis