an lead to  not being able to complete an entire  mission the mission brick in the wall is  an early showcase of the effective way  how all of these coexist together you're  sent on an investigation to find a man  named volkov you meet an agent whose  name is greta who provides you with  information of not only a man named  kraus but another agent of hers who was  captured this  is the optional objective of the mission  should the player choose to do this  they'll be given the choice of killing  or releasing the agent as well as  collecting the evidence for one of the  side missions in the future  the choice of letting him go or killing  him affects the future as it's  discovered he was planning on betraying  his current organization which is why he  shows up at the interrogation scene  while being interrogated the player is  given multiple options here too  should you cooperate nothing happens  other than scripted events but should  the player mouth off it can lead to  greta's death once you're saved you then  chase volkov to the end of the warehouse  where you're given the killer capture  order none of these options affect the  ending or the overall path of the game  but each option gives different dialogue  and reactions to your choice  that's three choices within one mission  which means there are many combinations  given to the player  some players may have saved greta and  her agent but killed volkov others may  have done  vice versa which makes the playthrough  more unique and fun to experience but  the true form of choice is easily shown  in desperate measures  desperate measures is easily one of the  best missions in the game you start out  as a man named belakov who was a mole  within the kgb  tasked with getting a bunker key so he  can let adler and bella inside  the only issue is one person has that  key general charkov the game gives you  five  options to tackle this all with their  unique challenges poisoning charkoff  seems easy enough but not only is the  poison locked behind a cabinet chargoff  also grabs the wrong cup meaning you  need to distract them in order to switch  them  alternatively you can reprogram a new  key yourself but the guard won't let you  pass without some convincing the level  provides you with a map and science  you're never lost and know exactly where  you are and where you need to go  even allowing you to mark sections on  the map so there's a waypoint and giving  you the opportunity to explore the other  possible  options should you want to the game even  provides an optional objective to kill  the man who wronged you just missions  ago which is a nice touch  while it seems easy at face value every  named location in the headquarters is  restricted thanks to the recent security  measures so not only are the guards on  high alert you aren't allowed to be  inside these areas either so you have to  lock pick your way through all the doors  and stash the bodies  once completing desperate measures the  players should have enough to finish  those side missions  operating chaos and red circus as we  discussed are the side missions that can  be completed right away but  it's intended for the player to solve  the puzzles to proceed with the mission  operating chaos has the floppy disk and  red circus has the finding of the  suspects these missions won't be solved  by everyone but it doesn't take a  scientist to figure these out  treyarch knew these would be tough so  they actually made multiple versions of  each of the missions so players couldn't  just look up the answers online  but instead have to look up how to solve  it and do it themselves preventing the  easy way out  doing it yourself is much more enjoyable  and rewarding it takes more thinking  than normal to figure it out  but it took me around 15 minutes to  crack each one treyarch handled these  very well giving the player a challenge  that may require minor note taking and  brain power but not too much thinking as  it would cause t