ime one scene is completed we see  glimpses of past events from our  memories before we're shot back into the  next scene  one is during the day then it's at night  then adler's the model for the enemies  then time is slowed down then there's  zombies then the laboratory is falling  apart nothing makes any sense that is  until the end of the mission when we're  told that we aren't who we think we are  we aren't cia  agent bell we're a russian soldier who  worked for perseus  back in the first mission we see arash  cap two people in the truck  we were one of those two people except  we lived and adler captured us and took  us under a program called mk-ultra which  was a real program used by america which  was a form of interrogation through  drugging and mind control which is  exactly what's happening to us we were  being brainwashed just like mason was  back in black ops one  and this whole time we thought we were  helping catch perseus but we were  actually being used for information  everything was fabricated our name  relationships and the entire document at  the beginning that we created  was faked we thought we created our own  soldier not knowing that this was a fake  report to get us to believe that we were  the ones who created those pages when in  fact we were something completely  different  this is not only a shock to bell but the  player as well the fact that throughout  this whole campaign  we are being lied to and used for for  their own gain is shocking to hear  which brings us back to that classic cod  theme of doing something bad to do  something good  adler in this case is like captain price  they want to do good but if they have to  get their hands dirty they'll do it  where captain price kidnapped someone's  family to get answers  adler drugged a russian soldier to force  out information adler used his own  memories of vietnam but twisted them  like they were ours so we can remember  that lifelong bond between the two of us  which makes it easier to trust him it  was then after that bombshell of  information we were given the choice to  choose  truth or lie i legitimately had to pause  just to think as there were so many  variables in play  yes we did get drugged but perseus is  killing innocent people so maybe tell  the truth but  belle was russian so his allegiance  should stay with russia so  lie constantly replaying these ideas in  my head as to what would make the most  sense in the scenario  the first option i chose though was the  truth i assume that after this was done  we would eventually save europe and then  hopefully i'd be able to portray adler  at the end of the game you can imagine  my surprise when i was almost 100  correct until the screen went black not  knowing if i died or not the ending made  me feel empty  not knowing who died or lived and  knowing that adler was going to betray  me anyway  even after i helped him despite what he  did to me when games have multiple  options most of the time you replay the  ending just to see both options  this wasn't the case i rebooted up the  mission not only just to see the other  option but  hoping this one gave me a satisfying  conclusion the issue was is i didn't  know what was going to happen if i told  the lie i assumed i wasn't going to  leave the room alive but you  not only were able to live but set up an  ambush which created one of the most  captivating endings in call of duty to  date once you meet at dugo you ambush  them and the final objective  eliminate your former team appears  that's absolutely gut wrenching  at any point in time you could have shot  your team but it's always a game over  screen this is the one time in call of  duty that you can shoot your own team  with no repercussions so it was a very  different feeling  it definitely felt crazy that i was even  able to kill mason and woods in the  first place two guys who have not only  been a large part of this current game  but the other previous releases and it  was definitel